      "position": {
        "x": -180,
        "y": -280
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 320,
      "data": {
        "title": "Contract",
        "body": "TypeGlyph reads named icon definitions `{kind: \"icon\", name}`, text/symbol definitions with value/symbol/name, as object definitions. Legacy graphs may contain bare strings, but TypeGlyph does not treat a bare string as an authored icon or symbol object. Text is limited to one grapheme by getSingleCharacterGlyph. Readers differ: surfaceChains extracts object glyph definitions; callers retain compatibility fallbacks. Do not assume every reader accepts every legacy form identically.",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
